WEBVTT

00:00:03.452 --> 00:00:06.057
Oh, yeah. I totally see it.

00:00:06.192 --> 00:00:08.062
VACAYTIONER:
Cannonball!

00:00:08.197 --> 00:00:10.024
SPRUCE: Running drinks
to the back two-top.

00:00:10.159 --> 00:00:11.528
Hey, Lenny.

00:00:11.663 --> 00:00:13.632
- Seaweed floats are almost out.
- Thanks, boss.

00:00:13.767 --> 00:00:15.036
Hey, yo, Spruce!

00:00:15.171 --> 00:00:16.532
- Spruce, hey!
- Specials are on the back.

00:00:16.668 --> 00:00:18.137
Don't order the clams.
Don't ask why.

00:00:18.273 --> 00:00:20.169
Fricassee squid
and one jellyfish slider.

00:00:20.304 --> 00:00:21.570
- Spruce, wait.
- Huh?

00:00:21.705 --> 00:00:23.474
Oh, no. I knew
this would happen one day.

00:00:23.609 --> 00:00:25.377
Listen, I know you recognize me
from BroZone,

00:00:25.512 --> 00:00:27.477
and I'm happy to give you
an autograph or whatever,

00:00:27.612 --> 00:00:29.248
but can you please
be discreet about it?

00:00:29.383 --> 00:00:31.751
Spruce, it's us.
It's your brothers.

00:00:31.887 --> 00:00:33.455
(chuckling):
Whoa.

00:00:33.591 --> 00:00:34.515
- Bitty B!
- What?

00:00:34.651 --> 00:00:36.289
- (roars playfully)
- Whoa. (chuckles)

00:00:36.425 --> 00:00:38.422
No tossing, okay? (stammers)
Too big to be tossed.

00:00:38.557 --> 00:00:41.125
The last time I saw you,
you were in diapers.

00:00:41.260 --> 00:00:42.695
- Diapers. Right.
- (chuckling)

00:00:42.830 --> 00:00:43.831
Wet willy! (yells)

00:00:43.966 --> 00:00:45.499
Stop it. That's disgusting.

00:00:45.634 --> 00:00:46.764
I am a grown-up.

00:00:46.899 --> 00:00:47.897
Oh, sorry.

00:00:48.033 --> 00:00:49.434
A wet William.

00:00:49.569 --> 00:00:51.005
Hi, Spruce. I'm Poppy.
Wow, it's, like...

00:00:51.141 --> 00:00:52.640
It's so cool to meet you
or whatever.

00:00:52.775 --> 00:00:53.941
Um, this is Tiny Diamond.

00:00:54.077 --> 00:00:55.340
TINY DIAMOND:
Hey, what's up?

00:00:55.475 --> 00:00:57.205
Killer nachos you got here,
by the way.

00:00:57.341 --> 00:00:58.873
- Yeah!
- All right.

00:00:59.008 --> 00:01:00.643
Okay, Spruce. We're here
because Floyd needs our...

00:01:00.779 --> 00:01:02.209
Actually, no one's
called me Spruce in years.

00:01:02.344 --> 00:01:03.411
I go by Bruce now.

00:01:03.547 --> 00:01:04.753
I'm sorry, did you say "Bruce"?

00:01:04.888 --> 00:01:06.319
Yeah. I wanted to put the whole

00:01:06.455 --> 00:01:09.252
"boy band" thing behind me
now that I'm a dad.

00:01:09.388 --> 00:01:11.257
Wait a minute. You're a father?

00:01:11.393 --> 00:01:13.659
Yeah. I can't wait for you
to meet everyone.

00:01:13.794 --> 00:01:14.996
Hi, honey.

00:01:15.131 --> 00:01:16.795
These are my brothers, unexpectedly.

00:01:16.931 --> 00:01:18.692
Oh. Oh! Oh, hello there.

00:01:18.828 --> 00:01:21.229
It's so nice
to finally meet you.

00:01:21.365 --> 00:01:22.697
- Hi! -Hey.
- Hello.

00:01:22.833 --> 00:01:24.803
This is my wife
and business partner Brandy.

00:01:24.939 --> 00:01:26.674
She is my soulmate.

00:01:26.809 --> 00:01:28.037
My very tall soulmate.

00:01:28.173 --> 00:01:29.343
But we make it work.

00:01:29.479 --> 00:01:31.145
How?

00:01:31.280 --> 00:01:32.741
We don't even really know
how it works.

00:01:32.876 --> 00:01:34.144
(chuckling):
I'm kidding. I'm-I'm not.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:35.444
I'm... I don't know.

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:36.751
Daddy, Daddy,
can I have a cookie?

00:01:36.886 --> 00:01:38.051
Becoming a dad was like a...

00:01:38.187 --> 00:01:39.888
like a seismic shift
in my brain.

00:01:40.024 --> 00:01:41.620
- Daddy, Bruce Jr. bit me.
- No biting.

00:01:41.756 --> 00:01:44.186
Daddy, I don't see how
any government stands a chance.

00:01:44.322 --> 00:01:45.487
You're not wrong, kid.

00:01:45.623 --> 00:01:47.026
I'm stuck
in this ketchup bottle.

00:01:47.161 --> 00:01:48.492
Okay. Gonna handle all of that.

00:01:48.628 --> 00:01:50.765
Just give Daddy
two seconds, okay? Love you.

00:01:50.900 --> 00:01:52.096
(clears throat) As a dad...

00:01:52.231 --> 00:01:53.600
Daddy, Daddy, Daddy, guess what!

00:01:53.735 --> 00:01:54.937
I have pink eye.

00:01:55.072 --> 00:01:56.504
- (trolls groaning)
- Oh, my. Pink eye.

00:01:56.639 --> 00:01:57.598
Oh, (bleep)!

00:01:57.734 --> 00:01:59.038
Look, Spruce,
got to cut to the chase.

00:01:59.173 --> 00:02:00.404
We're not here to catch up.

00:02:00.540 --> 00:02:01.743
We're here because
we need to hit

00:02:01.878 --> 00:02:03.210
the perfect family harmony.

00:02:03.346 --> 00:02:05.112
Oh, no. You're still
going on about that?

00:02:05.248 --> 00:02:06.776
Hey. Get these guys
their meals to go.

00:02:06.912 --> 00:02:08.843
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.
You don't understand.

00:02:08.978 --> 00:02:11.482
It's for Floyd.
He's being held captive.

00:02:11.617 --> 00:02:13.348
What? Well, then,
wh-what are we waiting for?

00:02:13.483 --> 00:02:14.815
We need to call the authorities.

00:02:14.951 --> 00:02:16.384
Hit the perfect family
harmony, ye... (stammers)

00:02:16.519 --> 00:02:18.259
Spruce, it-it has to be us.

00:02:18.395 --> 00:02:21.393
Floyd's being held captive
in a diamond prison.

00:02:22.227 --> 00:02:23.360
Oh. Well, yeah, you need

00:02:23.496 --> 00:02:25.030
the perfect family harmony
for that.

00:02:25.166 --> 00:02:26.894
- Exactly.
- Wait. But how?

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:29.104
We've never even come close
to pulling it off.

00:02:29.240 --> 00:02:31.606
You do remember our last show,
don't you?

00:02:31.741 --> 00:02:33.372
If we practice,

00:02:33.508 --> 00:02:35.740
I know we'll be able to nail it.
We have to.

00:02:35.875 --> 00:02:38.146
(chuckling): At my age?
I really don't think that...

00:02:38.281 --> 00:02:41.148
See, guys?
I told you Dad wasn't in a band.

00:02:41.284 --> 00:02:43.580
Oh, I was in a band.
I was in the band.

00:02:43.715 --> 00:02:45.886
You ask your mother
if I was in a band.

00:02:46.021 --> 00:02:49.157
Oh, he was in a band. (chuckles)

00:02:49.292 --> 00:02:52.126
(chanting):
Prove it! Prove it! Prove it!

00:02:52.261 --> 00:02:53.724
- Prove it! Prove it!
- Oh, all right.

00:02:53.859 --> 00:02:54.927
- I'll-I'll prove it.
- (chanting continues)

00:02:55.063 --> 00:02:56.329
I'll prove it right now.

00:02:56.464 --> 00:02:58.326
- Yes! Bring it in, brother.
- (cheering)

00:02:58.461 --> 00:02:59.966
Branch, get up there.

00:03:00.101 --> 00:03:01.367
Go sing with your brothers.

00:03:01.502 --> 00:03:03.238
I'll do it to save Floyd
when I have to,

00:03:03.373 --> 00:03:05.668
but I'm not doing it right now
just for funsies.

00:03:05.803 --> 00:03:07.302
Oh, yeah. Okay.
You're probably right.

00:03:07.438 --> 00:03:08.904
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:03:09.039 --> 00:03:10.741
You're the one who...
Wait. What'd you say?

00:03:10.877 --> 00:03:13.115
No, you're afraid that singing
with your brothers again

00:03:13.250 --> 00:03:14.710
after all these years
will overwhelm you

00:03:14.846 --> 00:03:16.516
with emotions too powerful
for you to handle.

00:03:16.651 --> 00:03:18.315
I-I agree with you.
I don't think you can handle it,

00:03:18.451 --> 00:03:20.022
so I think you shouldn't do it.

00:03:20.157 --> 00:03:21.418
I think I can handle
singing a song.

00:03:21.554 --> 00:03:23.290
(chanting):
Prove it! Prove it!

00:03:23.425 --> 00:03:26.161
- Prove it! Prove it!
- Ugh. All right, fine.

00:03:26.296 --> 00:03:28.025
But this is more than likely
beneath me.

00:03:28.161 --> 00:03:30.532
(cheering, whooping)

00:03:30.667 --> 00:03:31.893
♪ ♪

00:03:32.029 --> 00:03:33.729
♪ My girl's like candy,
a candy treat ♪

00:03:33.864 --> 00:03:36.136
♪ She knocks me right up
off my feet ♪

00:03:36.271 --> 00:03:38.237
♪ She's so fine as can be ♪

00:03:38.373 --> 00:03:40.403
♪ It's like a perfect harmony ♪

00:03:40.538 --> 00:03:43.777
♪ Candy girl, you are my world ♪

00:03:43.913 --> 00:03:45.407
(cheering, whooping)

00:03:45.542 --> 00:03:46.946
♪ You look so sweet ♪

00:03:47.082 --> 00:03:48.546
♪ Come back to me ♪

00:03:49.380 --> 00:03:50.746
♪ All I know ♪

00:03:50.881 --> 00:03:52.921
- ♪ When I'm with you ♪
- Yay!

00:03:53.056 --> 00:03:55.249
♪ You got the right stuff ♪

00:03:55.384 --> 00:03:57.322
♪ Baby ♪

00:03:57.457 --> 00:04:00.025
♪ Love the way you turn me on ♪

00:04:00.161 --> 00:04:01.622
♪ Oh, oh, oh-oh-oh ♪

00:04:01.757 --> 00:04:03.994
♪ You got the right stuff ♪

00:04:04.129 --> 00:04:05.631
♪ Baby ♪

00:04:05.767 --> 00:04:09.169
♪ You're the reason
why I sing this song ♪

00:04:09.305 --> 00:04:12.538
♪ You're all I ever wanted ♪

00:04:12.674 --> 00:04:16.640
♪ Baby, you're all
I ever needed, yeah ♪

00:04:16.775 --> 00:04:18.639
I can't believe this is
really happening!

00:04:18.775 --> 00:04:21.042
♪ So tell me what to do now ♪

00:04:21.178 --> 00:04:23.919
- ♪ When I want you back ♪
- ♪ I want you back ♪

00:04:24.054 --> 00:04:26.485
(scatting "Motownphilly"
harmony)

00:04:29.556 --> 00:04:31.693
♪ BroZone's back, all right ♪

00:04:31.828 --> 00:04:33.627
♪ Whether you're a mother
or whether you're a brother ♪

00:04:33.763 --> 00:04:35.761
♪ You're stayin' alive,
stayin' alive ♪

00:04:35.897 --> 00:04:37.762
♪ Feel the city breakin'
and everybody shakin' ♪

00:04:37.898 --> 00:04:39.798
♪ People stayin' alive,
stayin' alive ♪

00:04:39.934 --> 00:04:41.601
- ♪ Ah, ah, ah, ah ♪
- ♪ BroZone's really ♪

00:04:41.736 --> 00:04:43.398
- ♪ Back again ♪
- ♪ Stayin' alive ♪

00:04:43.534 --> 00:04:45.101
♪ Stayin' alive ♪

00:04:45.236 --> 00:04:47.534
(scatting)

00:04:47.670 --> 00:04:50.007
♪ I want you back. ♪

00:04:50.142 --> 00:04:51.941
(cheering)

00:04:52.077 --> 00:04:53.648
Ah, yes!

00:04:53.783 --> 00:04:54.809
We still got it.

00:04:54.945 --> 00:04:56.716
Oh, tell me
that didn't feel good.

00:04:56.851 --> 00:04:58.617
I can't believe I remembered
every word and every step.

00:04:58.752 --> 00:05:00.722
Looks like your band days
aren't behind you.

00:05:00.857 --> 00:05:01.987
(growls playfully)

00:05:02.123 --> 00:05:03.490
Um, Brandy, my love.

00:05:03.625 --> 00:05:05.756
So, I know we have
kind of a lot going on here,

00:05:05.892 --> 00:05:08.822
but do you think it would be
crazy if I were to...

00:05:08.958 --> 00:05:10.630
Uh, leave me here
to manage the restaurant

00:05:10.765 --> 00:05:12.760
and all these kids so you can
go on a musically charged

00:05:12.896 --> 00:05:14.361
rescue mission
with your brothers?

00:05:14.496 --> 00:05:15.730
Yeah. That.

00:05:15.865 --> 00:05:17.838
It'd be crazy if you didn't.

00:05:17.973 --> 00:05:19.503
You'll never forgive yourself
if you don't help your brother.

00:05:19.638 --> 00:05:21.269
- (laughing)
- And you can cover

00:05:21.404 --> 00:05:24.279
when I go on my girls' yoga
retreat next month, all month.

00:05:24.414 --> 00:05:27.412
But you should leave now
before you get pink eye.

00:05:27.548 --> 00:05:29.082
- Save yourself.
- Daddy? -Daddy!

00:05:29.217 --> 00:05:31.917
(overlapping shouts of "Daddy!")

00:05:32.052 --> 00:05:33.852
Gross! Love you.

00:05:33.987 --> 00:05:34.788
Quick!

00:05:34.924 --> 00:05:36.152
You got this.

00:05:36.288 --> 00:05:38.221
(Rhonda roars)

00:05:38.356 --> 00:05:40.762
("9 to 5" playing)

00:05:40.897 --> 00:05:42.596
(alarm ringing)

00:05:42.732 --> 00:05:45.200
♪ Tumble out of bed
and I stumble to the kitchen ♪

00:05:45.336 --> 00:05:46.929
♪ Pour myself
a cup of ambition ♪

00:05:47.065 --> 00:05:50.639
♪ And yawn and stretch
and try to come to life ♪

00:05:50.774 --> 00:05:52.937
♪ Jump in the shower
and the blood starts pumpin' ♪

00:05:53.073 --> 00:05:55.103
♪ Out on the street,
the traffic starts jumpin' ♪

00:05:55.239 --> 00:05:59.443
♪ And folks like me
on the job from 9:00 to 5:00 ♪

00:05:59.578 --> 00:06:01.578
♪ Workin' 9:00 to 5:00. ♪

00:06:01.714 --> 00:06:03.181
- Ow! You just burned me.
- (music stops)

00:06:03.317 --> 00:06:04.849
Oh, my God. I'm sorry.

00:06:04.985 --> 00:06:07.548
Um, maybe it would be easier
if you took your shirt off?

00:06:07.683 --> 00:06:09.116
Oh, don't be lazy.

00:06:09.251 --> 00:06:12.156
Oh, by the way, you know
that thing you asked me for?

00:06:12.291 --> 00:06:13.894
Space from you?

00:06:14.029 --> 00:06:15.456
(chuckles) Oh, no.

00:06:15.592 --> 00:06:17.330
Yeah, no. Uh, what?

00:06:17.466 --> 00:06:19.499
Uh, anyways, uh,
you said you needed a way

00:06:19.635 --> 00:06:22.035
to make your smoothies
even fruitier onstage.

00:06:22.171 --> 00:06:23.664
- You did?
- Shh. Yes.

00:06:23.799 --> 00:06:25.972
That is what I want. Go on.

00:06:26.108 --> 00:06:28.137
Well, I had an idea.

00:06:28.272 --> 00:06:29.508
Ta-da!

00:06:29.644 --> 00:06:31.076
Crimp, honey,
that's not an idea.

00:06:31.212 --> 00:06:32.340
Those are shoulder pads.

00:06:32.475 --> 00:06:33.510
I beg to differ.

00:06:33.645 --> 00:06:35.143
It's a high-powered vacuum.

00:06:35.279 --> 00:06:37.279
I finally put that
master's degree in engineering

00:06:37.414 --> 00:06:38.649
to good use.

00:06:38.785 --> 00:06:40.982
See? You just pop
the grape or strawberry

00:06:41.117 --> 00:06:44.559
or blueberry or guava slice
right in here,

00:06:44.695 --> 00:06:46.791
and it releases the fruit's
essence through here.

00:06:46.926 --> 00:06:50.660
Once you're onstage,
lightly tap this button,

00:06:50.796 --> 00:06:53.328
just delicately,
you know, like, once.

00:06:53.463 --> 00:06:56.736
(whirring)

00:06:56.872 --> 00:06:58.170
Oh!

00:06:58.306 --> 00:07:00.005
Oh, my God. Wait. Wait!

00:07:00.140 --> 00:07:01.376
(groaning)

